# ElevAIte — Career Horizon & Upskilling Copilot

A personalized, AI-driven career growth workspace for working professionals. ElevAIte continuously ingests developer profiles, runs adaptive turn-by-turn technical diagnostic interviews, and discovers vector-matched learning modules and live career opportunities.

---

## 🏗 System Architecture
* **Frontend**: React 18, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Lucide React, Firebase Web SDK (v10).
* **Backend**: Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Uvicorn, Pydantic, HTTPX.
* **Databases**: Cloud Firestore (real-time profiles & skill matrix), Cloud SQL PostgreSQL with `pgvector` (RAG vectors).
* **Google Cloud AI**: Gemini 1.5 Flash (diagnostic reasoning), Google Cloud Document AI (resume OCR), Cloud Text-to-Speech (audio commute digests).
* **Storage**: Google Cloud Storage (PDF resumes).

---

## 📋 Prerequisites
* Node.js v18+ and npm
* Python 3.11+
* Google Cloud SDK (`gcloud` CLI installed and authenticated)
* Firebase Project with Authentication (Email/Password) and Cloud Firestore enabled.

---

## 🚀 Getting Started Locally

### 1. Clone the Repositories
```bash
git clone [https://github.com/](https://github.com/)<your-org>/career-copilot.git
git clone [https://github.com/](https://github.com/)<your-org>/copilot-frontend.git

# Set your active project
gcloud config set project <YOUR_PROJECT_ID>

# Enable required Google Cloud APIs
gcloud services enable \
  documentai.googleapis.com \
  storage.googleapis.com \
  secretmanager.googleapis.com \
  aiplatform.googleapis.com \
  firestore.googleapis.com

# Create the resume storage bucket
gcloud storage buckets create gs://<YOUR_PROJECT_ID>-resumes --location=us-central1

# Create Document AI OCR Processor
curl -X POST \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth print-access-token)" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8" \
  -d '{"displayName": "resume-ocr-processor", "type": "OCR_PROCESSOR"}' \
  "[https://us-documentai.googleapis.com/v1/projects/](https://us-documentai.googleapis.com/v1/projects/)<YOUR_PROJECT_ID>/locations/us/processors"
# Note the generated processor ID from the output.

# Create BEsetup
#1. Navigate to the backend directory and create a virtual environment:
cd career-copilot
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate   # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

#2. Create a .env file inside career-copilot/
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=<YOUR_PROJECT_ID>
DOCAI_LOCATION=us
DOCAI_PROCESSOR_ID=<YOUR_DOCUMENT_AI_PROCESSOR_ID>
GCS_RESUME_BUCKET=<YOUR_PROJECT_ID>-resumes

#3. Authenticate your local environment with Application Default Credentials (ADC):
gcloud auth application-default login

#4. Start the backend:
uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080 --reload

# Create FEsetup
#1. Navigate to the frontend directory:
cd ../copilot-frontend
npm install

#2.Create a .env file in copilot-frontend/ with your Firebase project keys:
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSy...
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=<YOUR_PROJECT>.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=<YOUR_PROJECT_ID>
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=<YOUR_PROJECT>.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=...
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:...

#3. Start the Vite development server:
npm run dev

#4. Open http://localhost:3000 in your browser.